# Who reviews what.
#
# One owner means one catch-all rule is the whole file: everything falls to the
# maintainer, and GitHub's "no owner" warning does not apply to anything. Add
# narrower rules here when a subsystem gains a second maintainer — split by
# directory (`/internal/store/postgres/`), not by file, or the list becomes
# something to maintain rather than to read.
#
# The handle needs write access to the repository. Without it GitHub ignores the
# rule and stops requesting the review, and says nothing about it — which is why
# `internal/archtest` checks this file's shape: a typo here fails nothing, it just
# quietly stops routing.
